struggling under the weight of his  rucksack bomb  salman abedi spent two hours around  manchester arena  and adjoining train station before the  blast  trying to keep a low profile but he can  be seen on multiple cctv cameras  and his presence didn't go unnoticed by  some  neil hatfield was at the venue waiting  to pick up his daughters  at the end of the ariana grande pop  concert  he gave the inquiry a dramatic and  chilling account  of the moment he came face to face with  the bomber  sitting near the stairs to the main  foyer  i fought suicide bomber straight away  without  very little doubt in my mind it was  honestly my heart was racing  as soon as i saw him he was dressed all  in black he looked like a terrorist  it looked like he looked like a how do i  know how to explain it like a bond  villain the witness said he wanted to  call the police  but saw two security guards highlighted  in yellow and green on this image  and was convinced they had spotted a  baby and the police would arrive at any  time  he seemed frightened nervous agitated it  didn't seem right  and that that really my my heartbeat was  getting  faster and faster because i was thinking  this guy's moving into position to do  something now  but the police neil hatfield expected  never arrived  just minutes later a baby got to his  feet  and walked off to detonate his bomb  massive flashlight and i mean it was  like you know sheet lightning  it was like that filled the whole room  british transport police constable  jessica bullo  was first on scene but she admitted her  and a colleague  had taken a more than two hour long meal  break  when she returned to the arena she  missed a baby's arrival there by 10  minutes  if you had seen that man walking in that  way with that bag on his back  would you have regarded him as  suspicious if he'd walk past me  with that bag on his back i probably  would have asked him what was in it  the inquiry is due to hear from more  police and arena security staff  as a key question of whether more could  have been done  to better secure the venue is explored  in the days ahead  mark white sky news
 

